# NOTE: GitHub Pages IGNORES this file — it is here for Netlify/Cloudflare/etc.
# On Pages only the HTML <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy"> tags are
# enforced (no X-Frame-Options / nosniff / CSP headers exist there at all).
# Rule order matters on Netlify: the LAST matching rule wins per header, so the
# long-lived cache comes first and the HTML exception comes after it.

/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate
  Pragma: no-cache
  Expires: 0
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
